    "intro_html":  "Pot pie has one real problem as a meal prep dish, which is that a bottom crust turns to wet cardboard in the fridge. This version fixes it by skipping the bottom entirely and topping a creamy chicken and vegetable filling with biscuits, which hold up far better and taste better anyway. It bakes in a 9x13 and cuts by the square. Each serving lands at {{cal}} calories and \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
